# Google's C++ style, with two departures, both chosen by measuring the diff
# against the code that was already here rather than by preference.
#
# ColumnLimit 100 is where this code already sits: the longest line in the tree
# is 106 and three files exceed 100, so 80 would have rewritten 479 lines where
# 100 rewrites 238. Hand-wrapped 80-column comment prose is unaffected either
# way -- clang-format breaks a comment that is too long, it never joins ones
# that are short.
#
# AllowShortCaseLabelsOnASingleLine keeps `case kReq: return "REQ";`, which the
# switch statements here are written in throughout, and takes the reformatting
# from 238 lines to 195.
---
BasedOnStyle: Google
ColumnLimit: 100
AllowShortCaseLabelsOnASingleLine: true
